This paper examines the Hankel Sobolev space, denoted as $H_{
u}^{s}$, where $s > 0$ and $
u > 0$, utilizing a specific norm. We define an orthonormal basis for this space consisting of Prolate Spheroidal Wave Functions (PSWFs) associated with the Hankel operator. We present an estimator for a function $f \in H_{
u}^{s}$ by expanding it in terms of this Hankel orthonormal basis. We further establish that this estimator is unbiased and converges to $f$ in the $H_{
u}^{s}$ norm.
